Widescreen, side-on paths: fill the black triangles at the edges.

Reported after 0052: black triangles at the outer edges of 2D (side-on)
scenes - Snow Go's ice cave, the bonus rounds. Only kind 3 and 8 paths
change; forward paths behave exactly as in 0052.

Measured offline with the game's own camera, now decoded:
- position: the path point (0x80026A08);
- angles: the item after the path in the zone, 0x04B, two int16 triples per
  node, the first x, y, z;
- matrix: Rz(-z) Rx(-x) Ry(-y) (0x80017BC4), then row 1 times -5/8 and row 2
  negated (0x80017AF8);
- H: the path's 0x130.

The triangles are gaps, not wedges: geometry of the zone's own worlds that
no list within reach holds (1.5% of every side-on view's extra columns,
mostly where a path starts or ends). Lists of other camera paths hold it: of
the same zone, or of a neighbour zone.

crash2_wide_slst.h, side-on paths only:
- the pool: every polygon the zone's other paths and its neighbour zones'
  paths list, mapped to this zone's world slots by world EID. It joins the
  camera test's candidates after the nodes' own and is rebuilt when the path,
  the zone or the resident SLST entries change;
- a pool polygon is drawn only while it lies wholly in the extra columns of
  one side, so the 4:3 picture is untouched;
- a candidate with a corner the GTE cannot place (behind the eye, or
  H >= 2 SZ) is never added - it would be drawn as a wedge;
- the three side-on S000000F paths whose SLST rebuilds cleanly but does not
  end on its own end list (a data quirk; 0052 refused them) are used, node
  by node, where the game's list matches.

crash2_wide_geom.h: c2wg_placeable; the camera's data in the header notes.

Counters: wide_slst pool / pool_drawn (debug server and heartbeat);
crash2_wide_slst_stats fills 14 values.

Offline, all 3,069 side-on views (one node in four): extra columns missing
1.52% -> 0.45% (Snow Go 1.11% -> 0.02%), wedges 8 -> 0, the 4:3 frame as
with 0052. tuning/wide_frustum_sim checks 122 real cases on the game's
camera, 50 with a pool. Worst frame 0.74 ms, including a pool build; later
frames 0.04 ms on average.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake.

